+// MTS patch (player-saves.patch): living players survive server restarts.
+//
+// Setting mtsPlayerSaves (default 0 = stock: nothing here runs).
+//
+// With 1, every mtsPlayerSavesIntervalSeconds (real, default 30) and when
+// the main loop exits (SIGTSTP), all living non-ghost, non-tutorial players
+// are written to playerSaves.txt in the run dir (via playerSaves.txt.tmp +
+// rename, so a crash mid-write keeps the previous save).
+//
+// At startup, before the first connection is handled, every saved player
+// is rebuilt as a real LiveObject (through processLoggedInPlayer with a
+// forced Eve slot, forced position and display, no birth logging, then the
+// saved fields overwrite the fresh ones) and marked disconnected. The stock
+// reconnect path in processLoggedInPlayer then hands the same life back to
+// whoever logs in with the same email, and the stock first message (PU,
+// LN, NM, ...) tells the client everything.
+//
+// Timestamps (age, food timer, decay ETAs, cooldowns) are game clock and
+// are shifted by the outage when mtsPlayerSavesPauseDowntime=1 (default),
+// so being down doesn't age or starve anyone.
+//
+// A save older than mtsPlayerSavesMaxDowntimeSeconds (real, default 1800)
+// is ignored. Restored players who haven't reconnected after
+// mtsPlayerSavesMaxWaitSeconds (real, default 900; 0 = never) die as a
+// disconnected player. A bad save file is logged, renamed .bad and ignored.
+//
+// Included by server.cpp just before processLoggedInPlayer (after the
+// Time -> MTSGameTime macro, so Time:: here is the game clock).
+//
+// See docs/research/game-saves.md.
+
+#ifndef MTS_PLAYER_SAVES_H
+#define MTS_PLAYER_SAVES_H
+
